<BaseLayout
  title="About | Qixuan Ding"
  description="About Qixuan Ding: software engineering, research, mathematics, and community work."
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <div class="about-content">
    <section aria-labelledby="background-heading">
      <h2 id="background-heading">Background</h2>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          I’m an incoming Software Engineering student at the University of
          Waterloo interested in using software, machine learning, and
          mathematical/quantitative techniques to solve challenging problems.
        </p>

        <p>
          My interest in quantitative problem-solving has led me to earn
          national-level results in mathematics and physics competitions, in
          addition to three Canadian Mathematical Olympiad qualifications, an
          Asian Pacific Mathematical Olympiad qualification, and invitations to
          both Canada’s IMO training camp and Canada's national physics camp.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="research-heading">
      <h2 id="research-heading">Research</h2>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          As a research intern with a bioinformatics research group at the
          University of Calgary, I worked alongside PhD researchers and
          professors on machine learning applications in genomic prediction and
          genotype-phenotype association studies. I programmed and simulated
          models, analyzed experimental results, created data visualizations,
          and contributed to manuscript preparation. This work resulted in two
          co-authored papers published in the Journal of Applied Statistics and
          IEEE Transactions on Computational Biology and Bioinformatics.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="community-heading">
      <h2 id="community-heading">Community</h2>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Outside research and competitions, I founded and led Futurlign, a
          student-led nonprofit focused on AI awareness, impact, and responsible
          technology. I managed a team of 20+ leaders, staff, volunteers, and
          instructors and helped deliver courses and workshops reaching more
          than 400 young people in Calgary.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="interests-heading">
      <h2 id="interests-heading">Current interests</h2>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          As I begin at Waterloo, I’m strengthening my foundations in Python,
          C++, algorithms, statistical modelling, and software engineering. I’m
          particularly interested in machine learning systems, AI research,
          scientific computing, quantitative research and development,
          mathematical problem-solving, and software engineering. I’m always
          interested in connecting with researchers, engineers, founders, and
          fellow students working in these areas.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

